lzbt: install shim as the first stage (GjallarOS Plane 293 step 3)

Firmware with fixed Secure Boot keys trusts only the Microsoft UEFI CA, so
our own key cannot go into db. With --shim-directory, lzbt installs the
distribution shim (signed by that CA) in EFI/nixos and in the removable
fallback path, puts systemd-boot next to each copy as grub<arch>.efi, which
is the name shim loads, and installs MokManager next to both. Our key goes
into shim's MOK list; shim then checks systemd-boot and every lanzaboote UKI
against db + MOK. lzbt keeps the shim files out of its garbage collection
of EFI/nixos and writes a pcrlock component for shim (620-shim), which the
firmware measures into PCR 4 before systemd-boot. Without the option nothing
changes, and a former shim install is replaced by systemd-boot again.

Upstream: lanzaboote v1.1.0 (rust/tool). Queued for upstream in the
GjallarOS patch book (753).

